/*  The snake game — the vertical slice: a model in its own file, a clock in another, and a main
    that draws two frames with a pause between them.

    ⚠ Not a game yet. Nothing reads a key and nothing decides anything; the body moves because
    the frame number says so. What it proves is the structure — a type crossing a file boundary,
    a clock the game owns, and a blueprint that builds the three of them together.

    ⚠⚠ THE VIEW IS NOT ITS OWN FILE YET, and that is a language limitation rather than a choice.
    A module written inside a pull cannot name the pulled module's carried type in its own
    SIGNATURE — `given (the series of spot body)` is refused with "'spot' is not a defined type",
    though the same type resolves fine inside a method BODY. MEASURED 2026-09-20; see the ROADMAP.
    Until that is fixed the drawing lives here, where `spot` is in scope.
*/

Pull board.
    Pull pacing.
        For each frame in range 0 to 1, repeat:
            Define body as a series of spot.
            Insert cast board's at on (4, 8 + frame) into body.
            Insert cast board's at on (4, 9 + frame) into body.
            Insert cast board's at on (4, 10 + frame) into body.

            State "frame {frame + 1}:".
            For each row in range 1 to cast board's height, repeat:
                Define line as "".
                For each column in range 1 to cast board's width, repeat:
                    Define here as cast board's at on (row, column).
                    Define filled as false.
                    For each piece in body, repeat:
                        If cast piece's same-as on (here), the filled becomes true.
                    Done.
                    If filled, the line becomes line joined to "O".
                    Otherwise, the line becomes line joined to ".".
                Done.
                State line.
            Done.

            /* The clock earning its place: without this the two frames arrive together. */
            Cast pacing's nap on (40).
        Done.
    Done.
Done.
